@startuml Buy Goods - Activity Diagram (Main Success Scenario)

!define START_COLOR #90EE90
!define ACTIVITY_COLOR #87CEEB
!define END_COLOR #FFB6C6

skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam activity {
    BackgroundColor ACTIVITY_COLOR
    BorderColor #0066CC
}
skinparam start {
    BackgroundColor START_COLOR
    BorderColor #00AA00
}
skinparam end {
    BackgroundColor END_COLOR
    BorderColor #CC0000
}

start
:1. Buyer calls with purchase request;
:2. Capture buyer details & goods;
:3. Check inventory (IBM OS/390);
note right
  Very fast green screen application
end note
:4. Provide goods info, prices, delivery dates;
:5. Buyer confirms order details & signs;
:6. Create order in system;
:7. Ship order to buyer;
:8. Ship invoice to buyer;
:9. Buyer receives goods & verifies order;
:10. Buyer pays invoice;
:11. Record payment;
stop

note right
  **Main Success Scenario (Happy Path)**
  
  This is the ideal flow with no exceptions
  or alternative paths. All steps execute
  in sequence from trigger to goal completion.
  
  **Preconditions:**
  - Customer record exists
  - Customer address known
  - Valid contact information on file
  
  **Success End Condition:**
  - Buyer has goods
  - Company has money
  - Order recorded in system
  - Invoice sent to buyer
  
  **Performance Target:**
  - 5 minutes for order
  - 45 days until paid
end note

@enduml
